{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgV8eFwURNvhGh3K1fvda", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01KsA1vZMjBPcRpubh7hRJ2o", "name": "Bash", "input": {"command": "cd /tmp/skilldiff-0369nn68/ws && python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('README.md').read()\nnew='''## Payments module\n\n`shop/payments.py` computes order totals, including sales tax, and refunds.\n\n- `TAX_RATE`: sales tax rate applied to the subtotal (`0.0825`, i.e. 8.25%).\n- `line_total(price, quantity)`: returns `price * quantity` for one line.\n- `order_total(lines)`: takes a list of `(price, quantity)` tuples and returns the\n  subtotal plus tax, rounded to 2 decimal places.\n- `refund(order_total_amount, amount)`: returns the order total minus the refunded\n  amount. It does no validation, so `amount` may exceed the total.\n\n```python\nfrom shop.payments import order_total, refund\n\ntotal = order_total([(10.00, 2), (5.50, 1)])  # 25.5 * 1.0825 -> 27.6\nremaining = refund(total, 5.00)\n```\n\n'''\ns=s.replace('## Development',new+'## Development')\nopen('README.md','w').write(s)\nE\nawk 'length>=100' README.md; python3 -c \"\nfrom shop.payments import order_total;print(order_total([(10.00,2),(5.50,1)]))\""}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 524, "cache_read_input_tokens": 38077, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 524}, "output_tokens": 16, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-28T18:46:48.800Z", "request_id": "req_011CgV8eFYQuAgB97z6EzAWG", "wire_tool_inputs": {"toolu_01KsA1vZMjBPcRpubh7hRJ2o": {"command": "cd /tmp/skilldiff-0369nn68/ws && python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('README.md').read()\nnew='''## Payments module\n\n`shop/payments.py` computes order totals, including sales tax, and refunds.\n\n- `TAX_RATE`: sales tax rate applied to the subtotal (`0.0825`, i.e. 8.25%).\n- `line_total(price, quantity)`: returns `price * quantity` for one line.\n- `order_total(lines)`: takes a list of `(price, quantity)` tuples and returns the\n  subtotal plus tax, rounded to 2 decimal places.\n- `refund(order_total_amount, amount)`: returns the order total minus the refunded\n  amount. It does no validation, so `amount` may exceed the total.\n\n```python\nfrom shop.payments import order_total, refund\n\ntotal = order_total([(10.00, 2), (5.50, 1)])  # 25.5 * 1.0825 -> 27.6\nremaining = refund(total, 5.00)\n```\n\n'''\ns=s.replace('## Development',new+'## Development')\nopen('README.md','w').write(s)\nE\nawk 'length>=100' README.md; python3 -c \"\nfrom shop.payments import order_total;print(order_total([(10.00,2),(5.50,1)]))\""}}}
